„­bible_version£KJV¤book1§chapter¨sections—…¤book1§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆPaul and Timotheus, the servants of Jesus Christ, to all the saints in Christ Jesus which are at Philippi, with the bishops and deacons:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRgrace be unto you, and peace, from God our Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book1§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ-I thank my God upon every remembrance of you,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCalways in every prayer of mine for you all making request with joy,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ?for your fellowship in the gospel from the first day until now;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~being confident of this very thing, that he which hath begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÆeven as it is meet for me to think this of you all, because I have you in my heart; inasmuch as both in my bonds, and in the defence and confirmation of the gospel, ye all are partakers of my grace.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUFor God is my record, how greatly I long after you all in the bowels of Jesus Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book1§chapter«first_verse	ªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^And this I pray, that your love may abound yet more and more in knowledge and in all judgment;¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
