„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkbeing filled with the fruits of righteousness, which are by Jesus Christ, unto the glory and praise of God.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book1§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut I would ye should understand, brethren, that the things which happened unto me have fallen out rather unto the furtherance of the gospel;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSso that my bonds in Christ are manifest in all the palace, and in all other places;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvand many of the brethren in the Lord, waxing confident by my bonds, are much more bold to speak the word without fear.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book1§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNSome indeed preach Christ even of envy and strife; and some also of good will:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\the one preach Christ of contention, not sincerely, supposing to add affliction to my bonds:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKbut the other of love, knowing that I am set for the defence of the gospel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWhat then? notwithstanding, every way, whether in pretence, or in truth, Christ is preached; and I therein do rejoice, yea, and will rejoice.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book1§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrFor I know that this shall turn to my salvation through your prayer, and the supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑaccording to my earnest expectation and my hope, that in nothing I shall be ashamed, but that with all boldness, as always, so now also Christ shall be magnified in my body, whether it be by life, or by death.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ0For to me to live is Christ, and to die is gain.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^But if I live in the flesh, this is the fruit of my labour: yet what I shall choose I wot not.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhFor I am in a strait betwixt two, having a desire to depart, and to be with Christ; which is far better:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;nevertheless to abide in the flesh is more needful for you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd having this confidence, I know that I shall abide and continue with you all for your furtherance and joy of faith;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZthat your rejoicing may be more abundant in Jesus Christ for me by my coming to you again.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book1§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙñOnly let your conversation be as it becometh the gospel of Christ: that whether I come and see you, or else be absent, I may hear of your affairs, that ye stand fast in one spirit, with one mind striving together for the faith of the gospel;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡and in nothing terrified by your adversaries: which is to them an evident token of perdition, but to you of salvation, and that of God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnFor unto you it is given in the behalf of Christ, not only to believe on him, but also to suffer for his sake;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFhaving the same conflict which ye saw in me, and now hear to be in me.¦layout ªlast_verse